    "title": "Kansas State vs Baylor Initial Availability Report - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Drew Galloway ,\n7 hours ago\nJerand Bradley/Kansas State Athletics Kansas State and Baylor, along with the Big 12, have released their first availability report for Saturday’s 11:00 AM game in Waco. This will be the third report of the season for K-State who did it for the game with Iowa State and last week versus UCF. It will be the third for Baylor as well.\nNotably absent from the report, K-State wide receiver Jerand Bradley has missed the last two games due to an injury. It appears he will be a full go against Baylor. In other positive news for Kansas State, Jayce Brown only played a handful of snaps versus UCF last week before departing due to injury and is listed as probable for the game Saturday morning.\nThis is also the first availability report this season that has not included true freshman linebacker Darien Whitaker . He has not played a game yet this season. Another true freshman, safety Dominic Mitchell , was also out last week and is not on the initial report for this week. Offensive lineman Joe Vickers along with defensive tackles Holden Bass and Patrick Tackie are not on the initial report this week after missing last weeks game versus UCF.\nKansas State Availability OUT S – Colby McCalister\nLB – Ralph Ortiz\nK – Cub Patton\nLB- Zach Wittenberg\nLB – Maguire Richman\nOL – George Fitzpatrick\nOL – Michael Capria\nK – Leyton Simmering\nQUESTIONABLE WR – Adonis Moise\nWR- Bryce Noernberg\nPROBABLE WR – Jayce Brown\nFull Baylor at Kansas State Report",
